1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:01,897
Your website works.

2
00:00:02,335 --> 00:00:03,683
That doesn’t mean it’s safe.

3
00:00:03,999 --> 00:00:06,424
Behind every page,
code runs out of sight.

4
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:10,160
Brain Code’s PHP2Shell article
explores what happens

5
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:13,767
when AI helps uncover security flaws
hiding in that foundation.

6
00:00:13,897 --> 00:00:15,840
But discovery isn’t protection.

7
00:00:16,271 --> 00:00:20,480
A website can look perfectly normal

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:24,697
while the software underneath
still needs a security update.

9
00:00:24,827 --> 00:00:30,042
The lesson? Check your PHP version—
not just your plugins.

10
00:00:30,203 --> 00:00:34,002
So what does PHP2Shell
mean for your website—

11
00:00:34,238 --> 00:00:36,384
and where does AI fit into the story?

12
00:00:36,842 --> 00:00:38,249
You’ll find the link in the comments.
